# LEAF — a pinnate-veined leaf, top-down/iconic. Worked example of the Fronds op's FRACTAL
# venation (depth=2): primary veins branch off the midrib, secondary veins off each primary —
# the self-similar structure of a real leaf. Reference: the real pecan leaflet at
# assets/sprites/ref/flora/leaf_pinnate_venation_pecan.jpg (pale midrib, forward-angled
# laterals shortening toward the tip, irregular spacing). Source for a future herb/ingredient
# sprite when the gathering feature lands; for now the canonical Fronds usage example.
size 256x256
Background transparent

# the blade — an elongated pointed oval (smooth ~ outline), tip UP
Poly (0.50,0.90) (0.40,0.70)~ (0.365,0.45)~ (0.50,0.14) (0.635,0.45)~ (0.60,0.70)~ rgb=90,134,70

# the venation — FRACTAL Fronds: pale veins, mirrored both sides, angled forward toward the
# tip (ang→ang2) and shortening (len→len2), gently bowed, clumped/jittered/frayed by default.
# depth=2 grows secondary veins off each primary (sub = their scale).
Fronds (0.50,0.86)-(0.50,0.20) n=10 len=0.15 len2=0.05 w=2.4 w2=1.3 ang=46 ang2=66 mirror=1 bow=0.16 depth=2 sub=0.30 seed=5 stroke=150,182,112

# the midrib on top (pale, tapering to the tip)
Poly (0.50,0.88)@4 (0.50,0.17)@1.4 stroke=156,188,118
